const e="marthoma-ss-regional-talent-festival",d=2026,t="Built from the Northeast Region 2026 sheet (followed where editions differ), with the Southeast Region 2015 and 2017 rules added where the 2026 sheet is silent. The sources print no registration deadline, form, fee, contact person or news. The Southeast editions name the NIV 2011 (2015) and the NRSV (2017); the 2026 sheet names NIV 2011. Elocution is 3 minutes in the Southeast editions and 3 minutes 30 seconds in the Northeast 2026 sheet. The Southeast 2017 choir sings both English and Malayalam songs; the 2026 sheet has a group in each category.",o={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Mar Thoma Sunday Schools, Diocese of North America: regional Talent Festival. Read these rules before you register.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"The Northeast Region Talent Festival is on {{EventDate}} at {{EventTime}}. Venue: {{Venue}}. Your grade is the grade you are entering in September 2026. No electronic devices of any kind are allowed.",Notes:["Grade selection counts the grade you are entering ({{GradeBasis}}).","The Bible version is {{BibleVersion}}."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General Rules",Items:["The decisions of the judges are final.","Time limits are strictly enforced.","Breaking the guidelines leads to disqualification (Northeast 2026). The Southeast 2017 edition says violations are noted; the Southeast 2015 edition says they could result in disqualification.","The events are Singing in English and Malayalam (solo and group), Story Telling, Elocution and Bible Reading, with a Bible Quiz.","All participants and groups sing the selected song for their grade or group from the music sheets provided, unless stated otherwise. This applies to English and Malayalam songs.","Story Telling, Elocution and Bible Reading are in English only.","{{BibleVersion}} is the standard Bible used. (The Southeast 2015 edition names NIV 2011 for the quiz; the Southeast 2017 edition names the NRSV translation.)","The purpose of the regional Talent Fest is to give children a Christian setting in which to develop their God-given talents for the glory of the Lord (Southeast 2017).","Participants and teachers are kept fully informed of the guidelines, the criteria, the process and the method of assessment (Southeast 2017)."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Eligibility",Items:["The festival is for the Sunday schools of the Mar Thoma Church, Diocese of North America, in the region that holds it.","Classes are by school grade: Grade 1 & 2, Grade 3 & 4, Grade 5 & 6, Grade 7 & 8 and Grade 9 & 10.","The grade is the grade you are entering in September 2026 (Northeast 2026). In the Southeast editions the grade is the one in effect at the time of the Talent Fest.","Only one participant per Sunday school is allowed for each individual event.","Group Song and the Bible Quiz are open to students up to Grade 10. The Southeast editions say Grades 5 to 10 for the choir and the quiz."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to Register",Items:["For Group Song, tell the Talent Festival Convener which voicing (Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass) your group will sing.","The source does not print a registration deadline, form or fee."]},{Key:"dates",Title:"Date and Time",Items:["The Northeast Region Talent Festival is on {{EventDate}} at {{EventTime}}."]},{Key:"venue",Title:"Venue",Items:["The venue is {{Venue}}."]},{Key:"teams",Title:"Entries from a Sunday School",Items:["One participant per Sunday school in each individual event.","One group per Sunday school in each Group Song category, English and Malayalam (Northeast 2026). The Southeast editions allow one choir per Sunday school, which must sing both English and Malayalam songs.","One Bible Quiz team of three students from each Sunday school.","Southeast table of entries for each parish: for Story Telling and Elocution, one boy and one girl for Grades 1 to 4 and one boy and one girl for Grades 5 to 10; for Solo, one representative per grade, with boys and girls separate from Grade 5 up; the Malayalam solo has one representative in each of Grades 1 to 10; one Group of 6 to 12 students for the choir; one quiz team of up to 3 students from Grades 5 to 10."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Conduct",Items:["No electronic devices of any form are allowed in any event. No smart watches, headphones, AirPods, cell phones, laptops or iPads.","In the Southeast editions, participants may not use cell phones or electronic devices during the sessions of the Talent Fest.","Outside guidance or direction is not allowed in Solo Song."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging and Scoring",Items:["Judges' decisions are final.","There are at least three judges in each competition category (Southeast 2015). The 2017 edition says there are three judges for each event.","Individual items (Southeast 2017): each judge gives a whole number from 1 to 5 on each criterion. 5 is excellent, 4 is very good, 3 is good or achieved, 2 is fair or partially achieved and 1 is poor or not achieved.","Individual item awards by the sum of one judge's four scores: Gold 17 to 20, Silver 13 to 16, Bronze 9 to 12, Participation Certificate 0 to 8. The tabulation office gives the final award by taking the median of the awards from the three judges.","Group choir (Southeast 2017): each judge picks first, second and third. The office gives 4 points for first, 3 for second and 2 for third for each judge. The fourth position is computed only if needed. The choir with the most points is first, then second and third.","Judges sign every scoring sheet, note any violations and hand it folded to the designated staff member. The final computation is checked independently in the tabulation room before results are announced.","Each Sunday school may appoint an observer who stays in the tabulation office for the whole time. Only staff appointed by the office bearers process and tabulate the results.","Judges are encouraged to write comments on the tabulation sheet to help students see where they can improve. A Sunday school may ask for the comments of a particular student.","Time keeping: timing starts when the first word is spoken and the time keeper records the time until the last word. For a 3 minute activity a green paper is shown at 2:00, a yellow paper at 2:30, a red paper at 2:50 and a white paper marked OVER at 3:05. The time keeper gives the report to the tabulating office.","Bible Quiz: every Sunday school is graded by the same person and the scores are posted after each section (Northeast 2026)."]},{Key:"points",Title:"Overall Points",Items:["Highest overall score wins the 1st prize trophy. The runners-up receive the 2nd and 3rd prize trophies by the overall tabulation (Northeast 2026).","Southeast overall points for each Sunday school: individual items are Gold x 3 + Silver x 2 + Bronze x 1. Group choir and Bible Quiz are 1st x 6, 2nd x 4 and 3rd x 2. Overall points are the individual points plus the group points."]},{Key:"prizes",Title:"Awards",Items:["Overall: trophies for 1st, 2nd and 3rd place among the Sunday schools.","Individual items (Southeast 2017): medals for Gold, Silver and Bronze. Participation certificates are available to all other students if requested.","Group items (Southeast 2017): 1st, 2nd and 3rd place trophies to the top three scores.","Closing ceremony (Southeast 2017): churches are called in alphabetical order, with a summary of Bronze, Silver and Gold awards for each church. Students come forward and stand in line until all students from the church are called, then all participants from that Sunday school have one group photo. Applause is held until all names from a church are announced."]},{Key:"other",Title:"Not in this template",Items:["Southeast 2015 and 2017 print the same events; the 2026 Northeast sheet is followed when they differ."]}],Documents:[{Title:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines",Url:"https://nerssblog.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/talent-fest-sunday-school-guidelines-2026-1.pdf"},{Title:"Southeast Region Talent Fest Guidelines (2015)",Url:"https://njmarthoma.org/attachments/article/55/2015%20-%20Sunday%20School%20-%20Talent%20Fest%20Guidelines.pdf"},{Title:"Southeast Region Guidelines & Rules (2017 edition)",Url:"http://bethelmtcphila.org/CompetitionGuidance.pdf"}]},n=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, General Guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Only one participant per Sunday school is allowed for each individual event.","Solo Song, Story Telling, Elocution and Bible Reading are individual events."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:["Each individual is judged by the criteria of the event. In the Southeast editions the awards are Gold, Silver, Bronze and Participation Certificate."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Only one participant per Sunday school is allowed for each individual event.
- Solo Song, Story Telling, Elocution and Bible Reading are individual events.

## Judging
- Each individual is judged by the criteria of the event. In the Southeast editions the awards are Gold, Silver, Bronze and Participation Certificate.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Group Song and Bible Quiz",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Each Sunday school may enter one group in each Group Song category and one Bible Quiz team.","A group has at least 6 and at most 12 students from grades up to 10.","A Bible Quiz team has three students up to Grade 10 (the Southeast editions say at most 3 students from Grades 5 to 10)."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["Southeast overall points for Group Song and the Bible Quiz: 1st place x 6, 2nd place x 4, 3rd place x 2."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Each Sunday school may enter one group in each Group Song category and one Bible Quiz team.
- A group has at least 6 and at most 12 students from grades up to 10.
- A Bible Quiz team has three students up to Grade 10 (the Southeast editions say at most 3 students from Grades 5 to 10).

## Points
- Southeast overall points for Group Song and the Bible Quiz: 1st place x 6, 2nd place x 4, 3rd place x 2.`}],a=[{AgeGroup:"Grade 1 & 2",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details",Sections:{About:["Songs and topics: Solo (English) {{SoloSongsGrade12}}. Story Telling: {{StoryGrade12}}."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["This class has no Malayalam solo, elocution or Bible reading."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Songs and topics: Solo (English) {{SoloSongsGrade12}}. Story Telling: {{StoryGrade12}}.

## Notes for participants
- This class has no Malayalam solo, elocution or Bible reading.`},{AgeGroup:"Grade 3 & 4",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details",Sections:{About:["Songs and topics: {{SoloSongsGrade34}}. Story Telling: {{StoryGrade34}}."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["This class has no elocution or Bible reading."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Songs and topics: {{SoloSongsGrade34}}. Story Telling: {{StoryGrade34}}.

## Notes for participants
- This class has no elocution or Bible reading.`},{AgeGroup:"Grade 5 & 6",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details",Sections:{About:["Songs and topics: {{SoloSongsGrade56}}. Elocution: {{ElocutionGrade56}}."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["This class has no Story Telling or Bible reading."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Songs and topics: {{SoloSongsGrade56}}. Elocution: {{ElocutionGrade56}}.

## Notes for participants
- This class has no Story Telling or Bible reading.`},{AgeGroup:"Grade 7 & 8",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details",Sections:{About:["Songs and topics: {{SoloSongsGrade78}}. Elocution: {{ElocutionGrade78}}."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Solo Song has separate events for boys and girls (marked with two stars on the sheet)."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Songs and topics: {{SoloSongsGrade78}}. Elocution: {{ElocutionGrade78}}.

## Rules
- Solo Song has separate events for boys and girls (marked with two stars on the sheet).`},{AgeGroup:"Grade 9 & 10",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details",Sections:{About:["Songs and topics: {{SoloSongsGrade910}}. Elocution and Bible Reading: {{Grade910Portion}}."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Solo Song has separate events for boys and girls (marked with two stars on the sheet).","Southeast 2017: Grade 9 and 10 speakers may rely more on notes for an elocution prepared in the 15 minute preparation time and may use one reference Bible; smart phones and electronic devices are not allowed."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Songs and topics: {{SoloSongsGrade910}}. Elocution and Bible Reading: {{Grade910Portion}}.

## Rules
- Solo Song has separate events for boys and girls (marked with two stars on the sheet).
- Southeast 2017: Grade 9 and 10 speakers may rely more on notes for an elocution prepared in the 15 minute preparation time and may use one reference Bible; smart phones and electronic devices are not allowed.`},{AgeGroup:"Team Events (Grades 1-10)",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details",Sections:{About:["Group Song, English: {{GroupSongEnglish}}. Group Song, Malayalam: {{GroupSongMalayalam}}. Bible Quiz portion: {{BibleQuizPortion}}."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Group Song and the Bible Quiz are open to teams of students up to Grade 10."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Group Song, English: {{GroupSongEnglish}}. Group Song, Malayalam: {{GroupSongMalayalam}}. Bible Quiz portion: {{BibleQuizPortion}}.

## Rules
- Group Song and the Bible Quiz are open to teams of students up to Grade 10.`}],i=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Solo Song","Source":"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Solo Song; Southeast Region Guidelines & Rules (2017 edition), Solo Song","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The song is the one given for the grade, in English or Malayalam.","Southeast: the song does not go over one stanza and a chorus, or two stanzas for a song without a chorus."],"Rules":["Sing the given song as in the notation and the audio recording provided. No outside guidance or direction is allowed.","Southeast: the participant sings the given song only; the song of choice has been removed (2017).","Southeast: a pitch pipe may be used to find the starting note."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Reading from music sheets or lyrics.","Amplifying devices, accompanying instruments or external direction (Southeast)."],"Judging":["Northeast 2026 categories: Intonation (adherence to the notated pitches), Diction (enunciation and pronunciation of words), Tone (quality, consistency and projection of voice) and Rhythmic Accuracy (adherence to the notated rhythm).","Southeast categories, each scored 1 to 5: Intonation (accuracy of pitch), Rhythm (timing and tempo), Diction (articulation, pronunciation, breath control) and Voice Quality (steadiness, projection and power, tone, dynamics soft and loud)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The song is the one given for the grade, in English or Malayalam.\\n- Southeast: the song does not go over one stanza and a chorus, or two stanzas for a song without a chorus.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Sing the given song as in the notation and the audio recording provided. No outside guidance or direction is allowed.\\n- Southeast: the participant sings the given song only; the song of choice has been removed (2017).\\n- Southeast: a pitch pipe may be used to find the starting note.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Reading from music sheets or lyrics.\\n- Amplifying devices, accompanying instruments or external direction (Southeast).\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Northeast 2026 categories: Intonation (adherence to the notated pitches), Diction (enunciation and pronunciation of words), Tone (quality, consistency and projection of voice) and Rhythmic Accuracy (adherence to the notated rhythm).\\n- Southeast categories, each scored 1 to 5: Intonation (accuracy of pitch), Rhythm (timing and tempo), Diction (articulation, pronunciation, breath control) and Voice Quality (steadiness, projection and power, tone, dynamics soft and loud)."},{"Title":"Story Telling","Source":"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Story Telling; Southeast Region Guidelines & Rules (2017 edition), Story Telling","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time limit: 3 minutes at most. The time keeper's yellow warning is at 2 minutes 30 seconds."],"Rules":["The story is in English only, from the Biblical passage given for the grade. The story, with its title, can be paraphrased.","The storyteller memorizes the story and does not dramatize it.","Southeast: the participant stays standing in one place, with no running or jumping."],"Allowed":["Hand movements and facial expressions, appropriate to the Biblical story."],"NotAllowed":["Costumes (Southeast).","Dramatizing the story."],"Judging":["Northeast 2026 categories: Content (how well the story follows the Bible passage), Clarity (enunciation, pronunciation, voice strength and steadiness), Moral Application (applying the story to the world) and Presentation (memorization, audience contact, pace and voice modulation).","Southeast: the same four categories, each scored 1 to 5, with Life Application in place of Moral Application."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time limit: 3 minutes at most. The time keeper's yellow warning is at 2 minutes 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The story is in English only, from the Biblical passage given for the grade. The story, with its title, can be paraphrased.\\n- The storyteller memorizes the story and does not dramatize it.\\n- Southeast: the participant stays standing in one place, with no running or jumping.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Hand movements and facial expressions, appropriate to the Biblical story.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Costumes (Southeast).\\n- Dramatizing the story.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Northeast 2026 categories: Content (how well the story follows the Bible passage), Clarity (enunciation, pronunciation, voice strength and steadiness), Moral Application (applying the story to the world) and Presentation (memorization, audience contact, pace and voice modulation).\\n- Southeast: the same four categories, each scored 1 to 5, with Life Application in place of Moral Application."},{"Title":"Elocution","Source":"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Elocution; Southeast Region Guidelines & Rules (2017 edition), Elocution","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time limit: 3 minutes 30 seconds at most (Northeast 2026). The Southeast editions say 3 minutes."],"Rules":["The speech is in English only and is based on the Bible verses given for the class.","Southeast: the style is a traditional sermon of the Mar Thoma Church, given from the podium, and the speaker stays at the podium."],"Allowed":["Index cards or note cards. Hand movements and facial expressions, appropriate to the Christian speech (Southeast)."],"NotAllowed":["Reading the speech.","Walking while delivering the speech."],"Judging":["Northeast 2026 categories: Content (how well the speech uses the Bible passage), Clarity, Moral Application (application to the world and to the speaker's life) and Presentation (memorization, audience contact, pace and voice modulation).","Southeast: Content (structure, organization, opening, transition of ideas, closing), Clarity, Life Application and Presentation, each scored 1 to 5."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time limit: 3 minutes 30 seconds at most (Northeast 2026). The Southeast editions say 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The speech is in English only and is based on the Bible verses given for the class.\\n- Southeast: the style is a traditional sermon of the Mar Thoma Church, given from the podium, and the speaker stays at the podium.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Index cards or note cards. Hand movements and facial expressions, appropriate to the Christian speech (Southeast).\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Reading the speech.\\n- Walking while delivering the speech.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Northeast 2026 categories: Content (how well the speech uses the Bible passage), Clarity, Moral Application (application to the world and to the speaker's life) and Presentation (memorization, audience contact, pace and voice modulation).\\n- Southeast: Content (structure, organization, opening, transition of ideas, closing), Clarity, Life Application and Presentation, each scored 1 to 5."},{"Title":"Bible Reading","Source":"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Bible Reading","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bible reading is in English only.","The portion is given at the time of the competition."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Categories: Quickness (how quickly the passage is found and the reading starts), Clarity (enunciation, pronunciation, voice strength and steadiness), Presentation (pace, audience contact, voice modulation) and Accuracy (adherence to the {{BibleVersion}} passage)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Bible reading is in English only.\\n- The portion is given at the time of the competition.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Categories: Quickness (how quickly the passage is found and the reading starts), Clarity (enunciation, pronunciation, voice strength and steadiness), Presentation (pace, audience contact, voice modulation) and Accuracy (adherence to the {{BibleVersion}} passage)."},{"Title":"Bible Quiz","Source":"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Bible Quiz; Southeast Region Guidelines & Rules (2017 edition), Bible Quiz","Sections":{"About":["Quiz portion: {{BibleQuizPortion}}."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["{{BibleVersion}} is used for reference. The Southeast 2017 edition names the NRSV translation.","A team of three students up to Grade 10 represents each Sunday school.","The team writes the answers on paper provided.","Southeast: use only a blue or black ball pen; an answer that is not legible is marked wrong. The quiz master makes the final decision on conflicting views about a question, an answer or the grading."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Every Sunday school is graded by the same person. Scores are posted after each section."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Quiz portion: {{BibleQuizPortion}}.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- {{BibleVersion}} is used for reference. The Southeast 2017 edition names the NRSV translation.\\n- A team of three students up to Grade 10 represents each Sunday school.\\n- The team writes the answers on paper provided.\\n- Southeast: use only a blue or black ball pen; an answer that is not legible is marked wrong. The quiz master makes the final decision on conflicting views about a question, an answer or the grading.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Every Sunday school is graded by the same person. Scores are posted after each section."},{"Title":"Group Song","Source":"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Group Song; Southeast Region Guidelines & Rules (2017 edition), Group Song","Sections":{"About":["Songs: English {{GroupSongEnglish}}; Malayalam {{GroupSongMalayalam}}."],"TimeAndFormat":["Southeast: the song does not go over one stanza and a chorus, or two stanzas for a song without a chorus. Special arrangement of the introduction and ending is allowed if it is not longer than the chorus."],"Rules":["Each Sunday school can have one group in each category. The group sings as in the notation and audio recording; each group sings the stanzas of the song as in the chosen arrangement.","A group has at least 6 and at most 12 students from grades up to 10 (Southeast: Grades 5 to 10).","Churches may sing any combination of the written voices (S, SA, ST, SB, SAT, SAB, STB, SATB) that includes the soprano line. Octave changes and doublings only where written. Tell the Talent Festival Convener the voicing you chose.","Southeast: all songs must be Christian songs. The Malayalam and English roles of the mandatory song and the song of choice swap each year."],"Allowed":["Only an actual pitch pipe."],"NotAllowed":["Other accompaniment.","Gestures or actions."],"Judging":["Northeast 2026 categories: Intonation, Diction, Interpretation (dynamics, style, tempo, phrasing, expression), Rhythmic Accuracy and Blend (how the voices converge).","Southeast: Intonation, Rhythm, Diction, Voice Quality and Harmony, each scored 1 to 5. For the mandatory song no deviation from the given notes is allowed; improvements are allowed for the song of choice."],"Points":["Southeast: placing 1st to 3rd, with 1st x 6, 2nd x 4 and 3rd x 2 towards the overall points."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Songs: English {{GroupSongEnglish}}; Malayalam {{GroupSongMalayalam}}.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Southeast: the song does not go over one stanza and a chorus, or two stanzas for a song without a chorus. Special arrangement of the introduction and ending is allowed if it is not longer than the chorus.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each Sunday school can have one group in each category. The group sings as in the notation and audio recording; each group sings the stanzas of the song as in the chosen arrangement.\\n- A group has at least 6 and at most 12 students from grades up to 10 (Southeast: Grades 5 to 10).\\n- Churches may sing any combination of the written voices (S, SA, ST, SB, SAT, SAB, STB, SATB) that includes the soprano line. Octave changes and doublings only where written. Tell the Talent Festival Convener the voicing you chose.\\n- Southeast: all songs must be Christian songs. The Malayalam and English roles of the mandatory song and the song of choice swap each year.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Only an actual pitch pipe.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Other accompaniment.\\n- Gestures or actions.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Northeast 2026 categories: Intonation, Diction, Interpretation (dynamics, style, tempo, phrasing, expression), Rhythmic Accuracy and Blend (how the voices converge).\\n- Southeast: Intonation, Rhythm, Diction, Voice Quality and Harmony, each scored 1 to 5. For the mandatory song no deviation from the given notes is allowed; improvements are allowed for the song of choice.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Southeast: placing 1st to 3rd, with 1st x 6, 2nd x 4 and 3rd x 2 towards the overall points."}]`),s=[],l=[{Key:"EventDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date of the Talent Festival",Value:"2026-09-26",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, first page (Saturday, September 26, 2026)"},{Key:"EventTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Start time",Value:"8:00 AM",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, first page (@ 0800 am)"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Event venue",Value:{Name:"St Thomas Marthoma church",Address:"34 Morris St",City:"Yonkers, NY 10705",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, first page"},{Key:"GradeBasis",Kind:"text",Label:"Month in which the grade is counted",Value:"September 2026 (the grade you are entering)",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, General Guidelines"},{Key:"BibleVersion",Kind:"text",Label:"Bible version used",Value:"NIV 2011 (as used in BibleGateway.com)",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, General Guidelines"},{Key:"SoloSongsGrade12",Kind:"text",Label:"Solo songs, Grade 1 & 2",Value:"English: Nothing but the Blood of Jesus",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"SoloSongsGrade34",Kind:"text",Label:"Solo songs, Grade 3 & 4",Value:"English: What a friend we have in Jesus. Malayalam: Daivathinnu Shtoram",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"SoloSongsGrade56",Kind:"text",Label:"Solo songs, Grade 5 & 6",Value:"English: To God be the Glory. Malayalam: Yehova Yire",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"SoloSongsGrade78",Kind:"text",Label:"Solo songs, Grade 7 & 8",Value:"English: Praise him Praise him. Malayalam: Yesuve pole akkuvan",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"SoloSongsGrade910",Kind:"text",Label:"Solo songs, Grade 9 & 10",Value:"English: I will sing of my redeemer. Malayalam: Sthuthicheeduvin Keerthanagal",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"StoryGrade12",Kind:"text",Label:"Story Telling story, Grade 1 & 2",Value:"Zaccheus and Jesus (Luke 19: 1-10)",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"StoryGrade34",Kind:"text",Label:"Story Telling story, Grade 3 & 4",Value:"Prodigal Son (Luke 15:24-32)",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"ElocutionGrade56",Kind:"text",Label:"Elocution passage, Grade 5 & 6",Value:"The Encounter (Act 9:4-6)",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"ElocutionGrade78",Kind:"text",Label:"Elocution passage, Grade 7 & 8",Value:"Fellowship of Believers (Act 2:42-47)",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"Grade910Portion",Kind:"text",Label:"Elocution and Bible Reading portion, Grade 9 & 10",Value:"The portion is given at the time of the event",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"BibleQuizPortion",Kind:"text",Label:"Bible Quiz portion",Value:"Gospel of John and Book of Zachariah",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"GroupSongEnglish",Kind:"text",Label:"Group Song, English",Value:"Bring In the Sheep's",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"},{Key:"GroupSongMalayalam",Kind:"text",Label:"Group Song, Malayalam",Value:"Sthuthi Sthuthi",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines, Talent Festival Details"}],r=[{Claim:"Northeast Region Annual Talent Festival 2026: date, venue, events by grade pair, songs and topics, general guidelines, and the rules and criteria of each event.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Northeast Region Talent Festival 2026 guidelines",Url:"https://nerssblog.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/talent-fest-sunday-school-guidelines-2026-1.pdf"},{Claim:"Southeast Regional Talent Fest Guidelines 2015: events, rules and criteria, time keepers' report.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Southeast Region Talent Fest Guidelines (2015)",Url:"https://njmarthoma.org/attachments/article/55/2015%20-%20Sunday%20School%20-%20Talent%20Fest%20Guidelines.pdf"},{Claim:"Southeast Regional Talent Fest Guidelines & Rules (2017 edition): scoring and tabulation, awards, closing ceremony, entries per parish.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Southeast Region Guidelines & Rules (2017 edition)",Url:"http://bethelmtcphila.org/CompetitionGuidance.pdf"}],h={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:o,ParticipantTypes:n,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:l,Evidence:r};export{a as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,r as Evidence,t as Note,o as Page,n as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,l as Variables,d as Year,h as default};
